{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CK2Ht54GUaxsdNenUx7jAM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Rubric — week 4 writing response\n2\t\n3\tFour criteria. Each is either **pass** or **needs work** — never a percent.\n4\t\n5\t1. **Mechanism.** Names an outlier and shows why the mean moves and the median does not.\n6\t2. **Example.** One concrete example, not the class example, that carries the claim.\n7\t3. **Argument.** A single controlling sentence the paragraph is defending.\n8\t4. **Precision.** Uses \"resistant to outliers\" or an equivalent phrase; does not use \"average\" as a synonym for mean.\n9\t\n10\t## Growth\n11\tOne sentence naming the single revision that would most improve the piece.\n12\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65af77fa-b16d-418d-9c40-2d9bc98bf000","uuid":"1a14040b-2bf0-4a33-aee6-f981d9afd10f","timestamp":"2026-09-10T08:20:23.173Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/bear/Documents/CoWork/bear-textbooks/books/anthropics/claude-code-101/03-hooks-skills-commands/cc-grading-skill-definition/scratch/rubric/rubric.md","content":"# Rubric — week 4 writing response\n\nFour criteria. Each is either **pass** or **needs work** — never a percent.\n\n1. **Mechanism.** Names an outlier and shows why the mean moves and the median does not.\n2. **Example.** One concrete example, not the class example, that carries the claim.\n3. **Argument.** A single controlling sentence the paragraph is defending.\n4. **Precision.** Uses \"resistant to outliers\" or an equivalent phrase; does not use \"average\" as a synonym for mean.\n\n## Growth\nOne sentence naming the single revision that would most improve the piece.\n","numLines":12,"startLine":1,"totalLines":12}}}
